Story: Get told when the rate is right
  Approval: approved
  As a traveller
  I want to be told when the euro gets cheap enough
  So that I can exchange my money without watching the rate all day

  You are going abroad next month and want to exchange money at a good rate. Instead of
  checking every day, you set an alert. This tutorial also shows what happens when the rate
  provider goes quiet, because that is when you most need to know what the app is doing.

  Scenario: Set an alert, lose the provider, get the alert
    When the user sets an alert
    Then the alert is waiting
    When the feed stops answering
    Then the rate feed is unavailable
    And the alert is waiting
    When the feed answers again
    Then the rate feed is live
    When the rate reaches the target
    Then the alert is triggered

Story: Knowing how far to trust the rate
  Approval: approved
  As a traveller
  I want to see when the rate is old
  So that I do not exchange money on a rate that has already moved

  The dot next to the rate tells you how current it is. This tutorial follows a rate from live
  to late to missing, and shows what each state means for you.

  Scenario: A rate goes late, then missing, then returns
    When the feed falls behind
    Then the rate feed is delayed
    When the feed stops answering
    Then the rate feed is unavailable
    When the feed answers again
    Then the rate feed is live

Story: Alerts on a late rate
  Approval: proposed
  As a traveller
  I want an alert to fire even when the rate is late
  So that I hear about a good rate as early as possible

  Whether a late rate may fire an alert is not decided yet (see the price alerts topic), so
  this tutorial is proposed and is left out of the approved manual.

  Scenario: A late rate reaches the target
    When the user sets an alert
    Then the alert is waiting
    When the feed falls behind
    Then the rate feed is delayed
    When the rate reaches the target
    Then the alert is triggered
